From 9dd5e2afee79a1c0b091a46852ba78d641da9ead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:05:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-2b I2C data planes

Map the remaining six 2026-11-02 batch-2 Units onto controller-visible I2C
slave models, following docs/unit-research/2026-11-02-batch2-protocols.md.
Address/version conflicts stay explicit; every read-only fixture and every
rejected write is documented in the host catalog blocker.

- m5_unit_runtime: expose m5_unit_i2c_attach() so one Unit attachment can
  attach more than one I2C slave (a single Grove pair, multiple addresses).
- env (U001): DHT12 0x5c 5-byte frame derived from temperature-c/humidity-pct
  with a valid checksum, plus a BMP280 0x76 half that exposes only pressure-pa
  and reuses the existing US_BMP280 register/calibration model.
- ameter (U086): ADS1115 0x48 config/conversion registers inverse-derived from
  current-a (driver gain/rate/resolution formula), plus a read-only EEPROM 0x51
  with a synthetic checksum-valid calibration record (factor 1.0); EEPROM
  writes are rejected and counted (product page warns not to write it).
- extencoder (U161, 0x59): 4-byte little-endian register bank (counter,
  synthetic meter, reset, perimeter, pulse, zero-pulse, zero-mode, fw,
  address) with pointer-write/read semantics and address migration.
- ain4-20ma (U162, 0x55): 0x00 raw ADC, 0x20 current mA*100, 0x30 calibration
  RW, 0xFE firmware, 0xFF address; 12-bit vs raw16 and the page 0xF0 conflict
  stay UNRESOLVED.
- acssr (U139, 0x50): relay level, 3-byte big-endian RGB, address migration
  and firmware registers. This is a transaction model only; AC 24-480V/10A
  zero-cross/leakage/lifetime behavior is explicitly out of scope and must be
  a catalog safety blocker.
- gesture (U127, 0x73): bank-aware PAJ7620 register file, part id 0x7620,
  fixture-driven 0x43/0x44 gesture flags and 219-entry init writes accepted.

Offline QOM smoke (no guest firmware) validates property registration, fixture
read/write, range rejection and read-only rejection; no functional PASS.
